Title: THE GARDEN HAS A GHOST
Credit: Mochiichao Show EP01 - script v1 (dialogue-first draft)

EXT. GARDEN GATE - MORNING

A wooden gate. A new sign: GARDEN KEEPER. MOCHIKO (12) arrives with a backpack bigger than she is. The gate swings open BY ITSELF -- because MOCHII is bouncing on it.

MOCHII
New keeper! New keeper! You're late, you're late -- I've already watered everything TWICE.

MOCHIKO
You watered... the pond?

MOCHII
TWICE.

DOROWANI steps in, carrying a thick MANUAL almost as tall as Mochii.

DOROWANI
Dorowani. Steady hand, keeper of the manual. Rule one: the garden is glad you're here.

MOCHIKO
The manual says that?

DOROWANI
The manual says "mind the gate." The garden part is me.

INT. GARDEN POND - CONTINUOUS

Mochii stacks berries into a pyramid. Behind them, unseen, the pyramid UN-stacks itself, one berry at a time.

MOCHII
--and this is the pond, and this is the berry store, and these are the GOOD berries, and--

Mochii turns. Stares at the un-stacked berries.

MOCHII (CONT'D)
I stacked those.

A wooden toy DUCK rolls past. UPHILL.

DOROWANI
Rule twelve: everything in the garden belongs to somebody.

MOCHIKO
So who does... that... belong to?

KITTEMBER's flame ORB flickers hard at the empty air.

KITTEMBER
Something cold just walked through my tail.

EXT. GARDEN GREEN - DAY

GABU flexes into frame wearing a fishing net like a cape.

GABU
Ghost problem? Gabu problem. Stand back. I catch it by supper.

DOROWANI
You don't know what it is.

GABU
By SUPPER.

SPROUTLE is on the ground, cheek near the grass, looking at a trail of little FROST PATCHES.

SPROUTLE
It's not running away. Look. The cold spots... it's a path. It's pointing at the pond.

MOCHIKO
It's not haunting us. It's... giving directions?

EXT. GARDEN POND - DUSK

Five keepers behind a bush. The frost trail ends at the water. Gabu LUNGES -- splashes -- comes up holding pure SMOKE, which pours through his fingers.

GABU
Caught it! ...Not caught it.

Kittember's orb FLARES. A huge shadow rises on the mist -- tall, spiky--

KITTEMBER
THAT'S NOT ME--

SPROUTLE
That's my SPROUT. The light's behind me. Sorry. Sorry!

The mist parts. Small. Dark. Shaking. WISPKIN -- the garden's night keeper -- holding the toy duck like an apology.

WISPKIN
I moved your berries. I moved the duck. I didn't know how to say... I keep the garden at night. Alone. I wanted to be introduced properly.

MOCHIKO
Then let's do it properly.

EXT. GARDEN GATE - NIGHT

The keeper board by the gate. One name is being painted in, careful and fresh: WISPKIN - NIGHT KEEPER.

DOROWANI
Rule twelve. Everything in the garden belongs to somebody.

(beat)

DOROWANI (CONT'D)
And everybody belongs in the garden.

WISPKIN
Even the ghost?

MOCHII
ESPECIALLY the ghost.

Wispkin floats UP for the first time, smoke swirling, and rings the gate bell with its tail of smoke.

TAG - GABU still wearing the net. As a hat.

GABU
It's not a failed net. It's a successful hat.

= END OF EP01 =
